From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 09:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wowprospero: say why the code arena was refused.

With emulated TLS in place the translator runs, and stops on its own memory:

    err:wow:BTCpuSimulate DBT error -9 at eip 0x7bf33290

-9 is PW_ERR_VM, "the memory backend refused a request". It reaches the caller
from pw_x86_engine's first commit of the code arena, and carries no status, no
size and no protection -- place_above_guest and commit_code both answer every
refusal with NULL or -1.

The arena is the one allocation on this console that has to end up executable,
and a plain executable mapping is refused here: orbis_jit.c gets it by mapping
direct memory read-write and protecting it afterwards. Which of the two calls
